WEBVTT

01:43.460 --> 01:45.190
Yes, it's going well.

01:43.870 --> 01:47.250
18: "MitsuruLoid and Gyouna-kun"

01:45.190 --> 01:47.250
It's almost going <i>too</i> well.

01:47.710 --> 01:51.590
I suspect I'll be able to report
on its completion next month.

01:52.350 --> 01:53.550
The device...

01:54.170 --> 01:55.460
the Octovano.

01:56.820 --> 01:57.720
Allegro.

01:58.050 --> 01:58.650
Yes.

01:58.920 --> 02:01.710
I'll instruct them to hurry even more.

02:02.010 --> 02:03.220
Once the device is complete,

02:03.840 --> 02:06.260
we'll need only the power
of the father of music,

02:06.260 --> 02:07.480
the great Bach-sama.

02:07.480 --> 02:08.340
Father...

02:09.020 --> 02:09.900
Kyougo.

02:11.100 --> 02:13.240
You mean Professor Otowa Kyougo?

02:13.240 --> 02:16.060
Are you suggesting that we'll need
his assistance for our plans?

02:16.430 --> 02:17.500
Bach-sama.

02:17.500 --> 02:19.780
We've determined where
Professor Otowa is hiding.

02:28.580 --> 02:30.000
Unfortunately,

02:30.590 --> 02:32.900
our squad was taken out by traps.

02:34.250 --> 02:37.500
Professor Otowa has since
gone into hiding again.

02:40.560 --> 02:42.550
That's amazing, Mitsuru.

02:42.550 --> 02:44.600
Where did you even get the idea?

02:44.600 --> 02:46.770
You sure are a genius.

02:47.150 --> 02:49.250
This is an impressive article.

02:49.250 --> 02:51.770
I've never had such an excellent student.

02:52.290 --> 02:54.190
You sure are a genius.

02:54.230 --> 02:56.280
Mitsuru Akira

02:54.620 --> 02:58.030
A prodigy in the field of
artificial intelligence.

02:58.320 --> 03:02.050
We have the perfect job for you.

03:03.360 --> 03:04.530
Hello.

03:05.350 --> 03:07.700
I've been newly assigned here.

03:07.700 --> 03:08.730
My name is Mitsuru—

03:08.730 --> 03:09.580
Hang on!

03:11.500 --> 03:13.580
Let me know as soon as the
second hand reaches twelve.

03:13.950 --> 03:15.340
Okay.

03:23.440 --> 03:24.180
It's there.

03:24.490 --> 03:25.100
Good.

03:29.900 --> 03:32.650
It goes soggy unless you eat it right away.

03:32.650 --> 03:34.230
So, who were you again?

03:34.780 --> 03:36.980
I'm Mitsuru, the newcomer.

03:37.360 --> 03:40.220
Your name sounds like a dude's name.

03:40.220 --> 03:42.080
Mitsuru is my last name.

03:42.080 --> 03:44.900
Anyway, I heard you've been doing research on

03:44.900 --> 03:46.990
creating the ultimate musical instrument.

03:46.990 --> 03:50.310
I specialize in artificial intelligence.
Why did I get hired here?

03:52.970 --> 03:53.870
Are you listening?

03:54.100 --> 03:55.530
Yeah, I am.

03:55.530 --> 03:59.090
Actually, I was thinking
of making some humans.

03:59.570 --> 04:00.210
What?

04:00.690 --> 04:03.900
Nothing makes music

04:03.900 --> 04:05.630
better than humans do.

04:06.260 --> 04:07.470
Here's the blueprint.

04:08.650 --> 04:09.530
Isn't this...

04:11.260 --> 04:12.770
Why don't you publish this?

04:13.310 --> 04:16.870
This theory could turn the entire
academic community upside down.

04:16.870 --> 04:18.990
You could win a Nobel Prize.

04:18.990 --> 04:20.090
Because it's too much work.

04:20.600 --> 04:21.910
Too much work?

04:21.910 --> 04:24.200
Oh, damn it!

04:24.200 --> 04:25.110
Wh-What?

04:25.110 --> 04:28.120
Spices

04:25.380 --> 04:28.680
There was seasoning hidden
under the noodles!

04:28.680 --> 04:32.410
I can't believe I didn't notice sooner!

04:35.090 --> 04:37.830
I'm going to be the one to bring

04:38.230 --> 04:39.400
Bach-sama's plans to fruition.

04:41.520 --> 04:45.700
My personality and musical
intelligence generator software,

04:45.700 --> 04:49.710
MitsuruLoid, is based on an analysis and
evolution of the virtual Arkhedol app.

04:46.390 --> 04:49.050
Delicate <=> Bold
Rational <=> Emotional
Orderly <=> Chaotic
Isolated <=> Friendly
Analytical <=> Intuitive
Technical <=> Artistic
Deliberate <=> Spontaneous

04:51.080 --> 04:52.960
The prototype is complete.

04:54.830 --> 04:55.770
Bach-sama.

04:55.990 --> 04:58.560
Shall I prepare your car and
guards, if you're leaving?

05:00.770 --> 05:01.690
Don't mind him.

05:02.380 --> 05:03.900
That's just how he does things.

05:04.490 --> 05:06.640
He just wanders off by himself,

05:06.640 --> 05:08.780
and when he gets back,

05:09.310 --> 05:13.020
he has the outline of a piece that
gains the attention of the masses.

05:22.630 --> 05:23.380
Bach

05:27.100 --> 05:29.050
I see you're hard at work again.

05:29.740 --> 05:31.350
Have you made any progress?

05:32.810 --> 05:34.920
So you're learning

05:34.920 --> 05:37.060
about your own life.

05:37.060 --> 05:39.400
Are you studying the past,

05:39.400 --> 05:41.880
or are you studying your future?

05:42.360 --> 05:44.440
Quite philosophical, isn't it?

05:45.640 --> 05:48.300
Oh, I don't need to answer it.

05:48.300 --> 05:50.180
It's just a loan shark.

05:50.900 --> 05:52.690
How can I tell, you ask?

05:53.040 --> 05:55.960
I have a different ringtone set up for people

05:55.960 --> 05:57.730
I don't want to respond to.

05:58.350 --> 06:00.540
In that sense, music

06:00.540 --> 06:03.370
carries a lot of information, I guess.

06:07.750 --> 06:08.340
What's up?

06:09.000 --> 06:10.370
Do you see something?

06:12.970 --> 06:16.780
Man, I wish it would rain
money or something.

06:21.870 --> 06:23.900
I don't think any of it will sell.

06:23.900 --> 06:25.710
Quit shooting me down.

06:25.710 --> 06:27.940
Just watch, it's coming.

06:27.940 --> 06:31.010
I'm going to have a godly phrase.

06:31.010 --> 06:33.410
God's busy, too, you know, Sousuke.

06:33.410 --> 06:36.730
What would you know about God?

06:44.620 --> 06:45.980
What's up with this plot twist?

06:46.280 --> 06:48.130
Dude, this is escalating way
too fast for me to keep up.

06:48.130 --> 06:50.010
Come on. Anyone?

06:50.010 --> 06:51.900
Someone give me an explanation.

06:51.900 --> 06:55.310
Hello? Someone? Anyone?

06:53.310 --> 06:56.020
I told you to find me a musician.

06:55.310 --> 06:56.020
Hey!

06:56.280 --> 06:58.710
He creates noise unworthy
of being called "music,"

06:58.710 --> 07:00.710
annoying everyone around
him without remorse.

07:00.710 --> 07:03.390
He has neither talent, taste, nor humility.

07:03.390 --> 07:05.190
He's worse than a beginner.

07:05.190 --> 07:06.800
What am I supposed to do with him?

07:06.800 --> 07:08.020
I'm sorry.

07:08.020 --> 07:10.380
He was talking like a musician, so...

07:10.680 --> 07:12.010
Well, it's fine.

07:12.310 --> 07:15.330
He just happens to be a
resident at that mansion.

07:15.850 --> 07:18.340
I may have a use for him.

07:18.820 --> 07:20.110
Prepare the experiment.

07:20.110 --> 07:20.760
Yes, ma'am.

07:21.950 --> 07:23.390
What's going on?

07:24.090 --> 07:25.920
Kagura Sousuke-kun, correct?

07:26.650 --> 07:28.130
You don't need to worry.

07:28.430 --> 07:31.040
I'll let you leave right away, if
you give me your cooperation.

07:31.040 --> 07:32.140
Cooperation?

07:32.140 --> 07:33.720
It's easy.

07:33.720 --> 07:36.780
I just want to hear your composition

07:36.780 --> 07:38.310
through that microphone.

07:38.790 --> 07:40.950
My composition?

07:40.950 --> 07:44.570
Show us what you've got.
All of your talent.

07:44.570 --> 07:45.790
My talent?

07:45.790 --> 07:48.820
I get it. You're scouting me.

07:50.030 --> 07:51.900
Kagura Sousuke. Here I go.

08:05.630 --> 08:08.020
It's terrible, as usual.

08:08.430 --> 08:12.130
Now, if it's built according to
design, it should be any minute now.

08:20.270 --> 08:22.570
Where am I?

08:26.840 --> 08:28.820
Awesome song.

08:29.900 --> 08:31.310
It's a success.

08:46.880 --> 08:48.090
Warning
Wet Paint

08:48.090 --> 08:52.300
Warning
Wet Paint

09:12.760 --> 09:15.400
So damn hot.

09:21.790 --> 09:23.470
It's Gyouna-kun!

09:23.470 --> 09:25.570
My, he's so cute.

09:33.230 --> 09:36.040
Now, let's go, MitsuruLoid.

09:36.460 --> 09:38.210
Proceeding.

09:47.980 --> 09:50.480
Organic Cosmetics

09:52.580 --> 09:54.900
My. Welcome home, too—

09:59.190 --> 10:00.030
You...

10:01.080 --> 10:02.690
Why are you home empty-handed?!

10:02.690 --> 10:05.460
I told you to buy me some Calorie Off soda!

10:05.460 --> 10:07.330
Where are my gyoza buns?

10:07.330 --> 10:09.970
It looks like you don't have
my cream puffs, either.

10:09.970 --> 10:10.920
My potato chips...

10:11.280 --> 10:13.090
My gyoza!

10:15.590 --> 10:18.550
Potato Chips

10:16.020 --> 10:18.550
My, you've brought home a lot.

10:18.800 --> 10:19.940
Is it on you?

10:19.940 --> 10:21.410
You're quite considerate, boy.

10:21.410 --> 10:22.850
Thanks, Kagura-kun.

10:22.850 --> 10:23.560
Nice going.

10:23.810 --> 10:25.790
You are welcome.

10:25.790 --> 10:28.430
You're kind of awesome today, tool.

10:28.430 --> 10:30.400
Okay, move, please.

10:30.400 --> 10:31.880
Make way.

10:31.880 --> 10:33.190
That's a lot.

10:33.440 --> 10:36.410
I keep telling you to give
me your laundry regularly,

10:36.410 --> 10:38.120
not all at once.

10:39.000 --> 10:39.410
What?

10:39.950 --> 10:43.290
Don't just stand there, Sousuke, help me.

10:43.830 --> 10:44.370
Yes.

10:44.620 --> 10:46.960
What? Thanks.

10:46.960 --> 10:49.020
Where shall I take it?

10:49.020 --> 10:51.390
To the laundry room in the back.

10:51.390 --> 10:52.900
Acknowledged.

10:54.860 --> 10:56.680
He's pretty obedient.

10:56.680 --> 10:58.640
Is he plotting something?

10:58.640 --> 11:01.430
It's love. He's in love.

11:01.750 --> 11:03.170
I don't know about that.

11:03.700 --> 11:06.150
I can't believe they thought it was him.

11:06.770 --> 11:10.200
It goes to show how little
presence he has, I guess.

11:11.810 --> 11:14.710
When can I leave?

11:15.390 --> 11:19.250
Excuse me, may I leave yet?

11:20.040 --> 11:23.160
Maybe they're trying to figure
out how to do my debut.

11:23.420 --> 11:26.010
You're being way too positive.

11:26.010 --> 11:29.160
I don't think you're being
scouted to begin with.

11:29.160 --> 11:30.850
What? I'm not?

11:30.850 --> 11:33.110
Do you really think your song

11:33.110 --> 11:35.090
is worth scouting you for?

11:35.090 --> 11:36.680
You hurt me.

11:36.680 --> 11:38.300
That really hurt.

11:38.780 --> 11:40.200
Yeah, you're right.

11:40.200 --> 11:42.700
I mean, I know.

11:42.700 --> 11:44.440
I don't think I'm a genius or anything.

11:44.740 --> 11:46.860
But you don't need to say it like that.

11:45.090 --> 11:47.310
You're way too needy, Sousuke.

11:48.690 --> 11:49.790
Pops?

11:49.790 --> 11:51.580
Hey, Sousuke-kun.

11:51.580 --> 11:53.150
What are you doing here?

11:53.390 --> 11:55.840
I, like, got scouted.

11:56.470 --> 11:59.330
Never mind me; what have you
been doing all this time?

11:59.330 --> 12:00.700
Oh, you know.

12:00.700 --> 12:02.070
How's Kanae been doing?

12:02.070 --> 12:04.510
She's doing well. She's angry every day.

12:04.510 --> 12:06.230
That's good to hear.

12:06.230 --> 12:08.040
Tell her I said hi. Bye.

12:08.040 --> 12:10.650
Wait. I'm coming with you.

12:10.650 --> 12:11.660
What? Why?

12:12.330 --> 12:14.310
I'm done performing.

12:14.310 --> 12:17.420
I'm leaving now. Goodbye.

12:18.180 --> 12:19.360
Okay, let's go.

12:19.360 --> 12:22.290
Sure, but I'm not leaving yet.

12:23.660 --> 12:25.570
I still have some business.

12:26.260 --> 12:28.260
Whoa!

12:28.260 --> 12:29.040
It's really him!

12:29.040 --> 12:30.140
It's Gyouna-kun!

12:30.140 --> 12:31.120
Cool!

12:31.650 --> 12:33.020
Hang out with us, Gyouna-kun.

12:33.020 --> 12:34.900
Come on, do the Gyogyogyo dance!

12:59.560 --> 13:02.650
Hey, I like your outfit.

13:02.650 --> 13:05.420
Lucky you! I bet you're
a hit with the ladies.

13:05.420 --> 13:07.250
Wait, let me guess,

13:07.250 --> 13:10.030
you're actually a cute girl inside, too?

13:18.190 --> 13:19.380
How's this?

13:19.380 --> 13:21.650
This'll keep the kids from attacking you.

13:22.360 --> 13:24.950
Let me wear that later, too.

13:25.380 --> 13:26.570
Promise?

13:28.430 --> 13:29.910
Bach-sama.

13:30.340 --> 13:33.330
What a splendid day.

13:33.630 --> 13:35.260
Great Bach-sama!

13:35.770 --> 13:38.890
So it was because of that "Musik" thing that

13:38.890 --> 13:42.050
the presidents started
calling you "Bach-sama."

13:42.350 --> 13:44.450
That's pretty impressive.

13:44.450 --> 13:46.950
I bet you could even use it to

13:46.950 --> 13:49.300
make people forget that you owe them money.

13:49.300 --> 13:51.180
With my Musik,

13:51.180 --> 13:54.190
I can control people as I wish.

13:54.190 --> 13:55.620
I see.

13:55.620 --> 13:58.260
So, are you going to use that on me, too?

13:58.660 --> 14:02.570
Are you going to make me a pawn for
that Eight Sounds you talk about?

14:04.130 --> 14:06.140
The Eight Sounds is my ultimate goal.

14:06.500 --> 14:09.270
I will achieve it by any means.

14:09.270 --> 14:11.560
To that end, Kyougo,

14:13.000 --> 14:14.290
I need you.

14:15.990 --> 14:17.770
I'm asking for your help.

14:18.280 --> 14:21.040
Not as a pawn, but as a supporter.

14:23.570 --> 14:25.100
Got it. Yeah.

14:25.100 --> 14:27.600
But this is a huge decision.

14:27.900 --> 14:30.470
Would you give me an hour
to make up my mind?

14:32.660 --> 14:33.730
Thanks.

14:33.730 --> 14:36.020
I'll do my best to give
you a positive answer.

14:36.410 --> 14:37.480
I promise.

14:38.870 --> 14:40.230
Now, then...

14:40.230 --> 14:42.690
I guess there are only <i>those</i> two
that I can wake up right away.

14:43.200 --> 14:44.880
Ah, well, it'll have to do.

14:46.800 --> 14:49.530
How do you feel to be awake, Beethes?

14:50.030 --> 14:50.890
Beethes?

14:51.230 --> 14:52.740
My name is Ludwig van...

14:52.740 --> 14:54.540
Beethes is fine.

14:55.080 --> 14:56.860
And you're Motes.

14:56.860 --> 14:57.620
Motes?

14:58.410 --> 15:02.270
I hate to get straight to business,
but I need you two to come with me.

15:04.080 --> 15:05.060
They've escaped!

15:05.060 --> 15:06.040
That way!

15:15.870 --> 15:19.810
So this place was an
Arkhe research facility.

15:20.350 --> 15:23.320
I used to work here, at
this research facility.

15:24.010 --> 15:25.320
Why are you here today?

15:25.770 --> 15:28.080
I'm here to pick up something I left behind.

15:35.490 --> 15:36.870
He sure is hard-working.

15:37.110 --> 15:38.110
I know.

15:38.110 --> 15:39.860
It's like he's been reborn.

15:39.860 --> 15:43.840
A boy can sometimes mature drastically.

15:52.230 --> 15:53.470
Damn it!

15:53.470 --> 15:55.540
What the hell are you doing, Sousuke?

15:55.540 --> 15:57.850
A tool is a tool, after all.

15:57.850 --> 15:59.880
Alas, he's no different from usual.

15:59.880 --> 16:01.620
His youth ends here!

16:01.620 --> 16:03.730
It's all downhill from here.

16:04.150 --> 16:05.360
He's done.

16:08.460 --> 16:11.530
I desire praise.

16:11.790 --> 16:12.420
Huh?

16:12.420 --> 16:13.200
Say what?

16:13.620 --> 16:23.420
Praise me more.

16:20.120 --> 16:22.420
Is this Musik?

16:22.420 --> 16:23.420
Stop it!

16:25.130 --> 16:27.170
Sousuke!

16:27.170 --> 16:28.120
After him!

16:28.830 --> 16:34.050
Praise me!

16:34.300 --> 16:36.860
I think we've lost them now.

16:36.860 --> 16:38.240
No kids here, either.

16:40.030 --> 16:40.970
What's going on?

16:41.270 --> 16:42.230
Beef Bowl Gold

16:41.270 --> 16:43.100
Praise me!

16:43.360 --> 16:45.940
Praise me!

16:46.190 --> 16:47.900
Huh? Sousuke.

16:49.270 --> 16:50.740
Where are we?

16:51.510 --> 16:52.400
It says something.

16:52.740 --> 16:53.380
V...?

16:53.730 --> 16:54.580
V...?

16:54.580 --> 16:55.660
"Beethoven."

16:55.990 --> 16:58.370
And it says "Mozart" on the next one.

16:59.150 --> 17:01.840
What exactly did you leave behind, Pops?

17:02.590 --> 17:03.330
Found it!

17:03.670 --> 17:05.960
Man, thank goodness.

17:05.960 --> 17:09.210
I was, like, what if someone
had already found it?

17:09.920 --> 17:12.070
I'm out of spending money.

17:12.070 --> 17:14.590
I was trying to figure out how to buy dinner,

17:14.590 --> 17:15.970
when I remembered this.

17:15.970 --> 17:18.220
I remembered I had a secret stash here.

17:18.220 --> 17:19.510
A secret stash?

17:19.510 --> 17:20.590
1000 yen?

17:20.940 --> 17:22.960
You came all the way here just for that?

17:22.960 --> 17:23.550
Yeah.

17:23.550 --> 17:24.740
"Yeah"?

17:24.740 --> 17:27.160
Don't you scoff at 1000 yen.

17:27.730 --> 17:31.270
I can live off of 1000 yen for a week.

17:31.770 --> 17:33.080
Okay, let's leave.

17:33.460 --> 17:34.800
Right.

17:39.130 --> 17:41.830
Professor Otowa! What are you doing here?

17:42.150 --> 17:43.730
Hey, Mitsuru-kun.

17:43.730 --> 17:46.060
I didn't steal this or anything.

17:46.060 --> 17:47.130
This was always—

17:47.130 --> 17:49.070
You left Bach-sama behind,

17:49.070 --> 17:51.260
and you had the gall to walk right back in.

17:51.260 --> 17:52.710
Do you think we're that stupid?

17:52.710 --> 17:54.330
The way you talk...

17:54.330 --> 17:55.590
You're the one who scouted me!

17:55.940 --> 17:58.910
It looks like Bach-sama made a huge
mistake, putting his faith in you.

17:59.210 --> 18:02.030
You don't belong here anymore.

18:02.740 --> 18:04.460
You remember

18:04.460 --> 18:06.990
that I hid my stash there, too, right?

18:06.990 --> 18:09.940
I mean, if you <i>really</i> insist,
I'll give you ten percent.

18:09.940 --> 18:13.340
I'm going to be the one to
complete Bach-sama's plan.

18:13.340 --> 18:17.380
Using an entity even more evolved
than the ClassicaLoids you created.

18:17.380 --> 18:20.420
But think about it. I'm jobless right now.

18:20.420 --> 18:22.610
How just is it to take

18:22.610 --> 18:24.970
100 yen from me right now?

18:24.970 --> 18:26.400
Their conversation...

18:26.400 --> 18:28.000
...isn't very coherent.

18:31.260 --> 18:32.380
The MitsuruLoid?

18:32.660 --> 18:33.970
I'll be right there.

18:34.710 --> 18:36.380
Did something happen?

18:36.380 --> 18:38.210
Okay, let's get going.

18:39.000 --> 18:44.390
Praise me!

18:44.680 --> 18:46.190
It's Gyouna-kun!

18:46.190 --> 18:47.310
Gyouna-kun!

18:47.310 --> 18:49.410
Hey, it <i>is</i> Sousuke.

18:49.410 --> 18:51.510
Hey! What's up?

18:51.510 --> 18:56.280
Praise me!

19:00.280 --> 19:01.910
Praise me!

19:01.910 --> 19:07.400
Fühle meine Musik!

19:16.580 --> 19:18.640
Quit bullying kids, Sousuke!

19:18.640 --> 19:19.590
There he is!

19:19.900 --> 19:21.400
Lud-kun.

19:21.400 --> 19:22.520
Wolf.

19:22.520 --> 19:26.890
Praise me!

19:25.140 --> 19:26.890
Don't push it, boy!

19:27.140 --> 19:31.440
Spielen wir unsere Musik!

19:36.490 --> 19:40.150
Your behavior is not worthy of praise!

19:40.950 --> 19:46.540
Praise me!

19:42.950 --> 19:44.070
Seriously!

19:45.650 --> 19:46.540
Say...

19:46.540 --> 19:50.020
Don't you think their Musik
is different than usual?

19:50.020 --> 19:51.040
How so?

19:52.790 --> 19:54.180
It's proper.

19:55.050 --> 19:56.310
I know.

19:56.310 --> 19:58.760
They have proper control over it.

19:58.760 --> 20:00.970
They're totally coordinating, too.

20:02.350 --> 20:03.450
Of course.

20:03.450 --> 20:05.830
Beethoven-senpai is a genius, after all.

20:06.130 --> 20:08.560
Mozart is just fluking out.

20:09.210 --> 20:11.060
You're right. It's just a fluke.

20:11.390 --> 20:14.150
Mo— More...

20:14.150 --> 20:20.660
Praise me more!

20:21.770 --> 20:26.560
Praise me more!

20:26.560 --> 20:30.870
Praise me more!

20:33.020 --> 20:35.440
Fuege Dich zusammen

20:36.510 --> 20:39.410
meine Melodie!

21:02.660 --> 21:04.240
More...

21:05.240 --> 21:05.910
Huh?

21:08.650 --> 21:11.290
Praise me more...

21:11.720 --> 21:15.160
Praise me more...

21:27.240 --> 21:28.430
Sousuke!

21:28.730 --> 21:29.710
Sousuke!

21:31.290 --> 21:32.130
Yeah?

21:32.730 --> 21:35.200
Sousuke. Why are you here?

21:35.200 --> 21:36.440
Why?

21:36.440 --> 21:38.680
I heard the commotion.

21:38.680 --> 21:40.480
No, wait,

21:40.480 --> 21:42.930
who do you think I was with just now?

21:42.930 --> 21:44.300
I was with your Pops.

21:44.300 --> 21:45.780
Your dad.

21:46.420 --> 21:48.410
My dad? No way.

21:48.410 --> 21:49.380
Really.

21:49.380 --> 21:52.030
We came here together from the
mountains way over there.

21:52.030 --> 21:53.370
So where's Dad?

21:53.610 --> 21:55.230
We got to the station, and he was, like,

21:55.230 --> 21:58.150
"Say hi to Kanae for me,"
and then he left somewhere.

21:58.150 --> 22:00.950
Why didn't you stop him?!

22:00.950 --> 22:03.170
Ow! Let me go!

22:04.150 --> 22:05.460
He looks real.

22:05.460 --> 22:07.390
He has Pad-kun with him, too.

22:07.390 --> 22:08.370
What?

22:08.370 --> 22:09.430
Then who's that?

22:10.910 --> 22:11.730
He's gone.

22:11.730 --> 22:12.870
Huh?

22:12.870 --> 22:14.480
Where's the animal suit guy?

22:14.700 --> 22:17.940
I have no idea what's going on.

22:27.880 --> 22:31.370
There's still room for improvement.

22:33.450 --> 22:35.830
Just wait, Bach-sama.

22:43.000 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

24:15.970 --> 24:25.400
Love, And You Shall Die

24:16.290 --> 24:19.170
Much of what the world
believes is but fantasy.

24:19.170 --> 24:20.810
Misunderstanding, misinformation,
misconception.

24:20.810 --> 24:22.730
Ultimately, nothing but jealousy.

24:22.730 --> 24:26.230
Passions pass each other by, only to find
themselves back-to-back in the darkness.

24:26.230 --> 24:29.220
The key to restoration is serious Musik.
